This repository also holds material that comes from, or describes, OpenAI's ChatGPT desktop app and its Codex app-server. It is
included only so the framework can work with the app the user already has (interoperability), and it is not covered by this
project's MIT License:

- framework/renderer/present/kit/glyphs.mjs: line glyphs taken from the app's interface, so that mods drawn with the framework's
  kit match the app they run in.
- adapters/*/adapter.json, build-facts.json, refresh-report.json and NOTES.md: per-build facts about the app's bundle (its
  routes, components and message types) and short fragments of its code that the builder uses as patch anchors, to modify a copy
  the user builds from their own installed app. The stock app itself is never modified or redistributed.
- contracts/upstream/: the app-server protocol's JSON schemas and TypeScript types, as generated by the Codex CLI's app-server
  (`codex app-server generate-json-schema` / `generate-ts`) bundled in the app. The Codex CLI is published by OpenAI at
  https://github.com/openai/codex under its own license.
- tests/fixtures/captures/: sanitized recordings of the app-server protocol, with synthetic identifiers and paths.

Each user builds their own copy of the app from their own stock app; no part of the app is distributed by this project. If you hold
rights in any of this material and want it removed, open an issue or report it privately (SECURITY.md).
